# The working-protocol approval state, and the only part of the enforcement
# that stays local. It is per-session authorization rather than configuration:
# `approved` names the plan currently authorized, `pending` is the block the
# user is about to apply, and the two override files are one-shot by design and
# deleted as they are consumed. Committing any of them would turn a decision
# taken once into a standing permission, shared with every clone.
#
# The gate itself, its wiring, and the instruction files are tracked. They hold
# logic and instructions, not secrets, and keeping them out of git cost more
# than it bought: a change to the detector left no trace in any diff, a fresh
# clone was ungoverned without saying so, and the obscurity only ever defended
# against content that could guess the word "approved" anyway.
.claude/protocol/
docs/dev/WORKING-INSTRUCTIONS.md

# Local-only ideation note; the rest of docs/scratch/ stays tracked
docs/scratch/ASSURANCE-ANCHORED-PARAMETERS.md

# Frozen design prototype for the FB-F valuation shape. Kept local: it is a
# sketch that answers "what type shape", not production code, and nothing in
# it is fit to be transcribed. The transplant works from production's own
# idioms with the prototype as the shape reference only.
docs/scratch/valuation-prototypes/
